WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.936
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.200
Ideas are everything.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.060
We're nothing without an idea.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:18.090
So I go where the ideas lead.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.420
When we get an
idea that we love,

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.120
you see it and feel it
and know it all at once.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:30.330
A desire for an idea is like
putting a little piece of bait

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.790
on a hook and lowering
it into the water.

00:00:37.062 --> 00:00:38.770
You don't know when
they're going to come

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.180
or what will trigger them.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.930
Lo and behold, on a
lucky day, bingo-- you'll

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:49.330
catch an idea, and party time.

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:54.190
If you want to make a feature
length film, all you need to do

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:56.890
is get 70 ideas.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.080
And you write these scenes
on three-by-five cards.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.660
Then when you have 70 of them,
you've got a feature film.

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:06.850
Find your own voice.

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:13.170
Never give up final cut
and total creative freedom.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.580
Everything is connected
in some way or another.

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:21.223
You could be working
on a painting,

00:01:21.223 --> 00:01:27.820
and suddenly, something in that
gives you an idea for a film.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:33.496
Music, painting, cinema--
this is the art life.

00:01:33.496 --> 00:01:38.820
In cinema, I don't like rules.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:44.314
In "Mulholland Drive," we
only had one shot left to get.

00:01:44.314 --> 00:01:45.990
WOMAN: How did you get it?

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.280
 By breaking the rules.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.710
[CHUCKLES] My name
is David Lynch,

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:55.110
and this is my MasterClass.

